hadiths[140]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1581","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah refuses to grant repentance to the killer of a believer."
"1582","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, called the Ansar and said: Is there anyone among you other than yourselves? They said: No, except a nephew of ours. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The nephew of a people is from them."
"1583","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, after he stoned the Aslami, said: Avoid this abomination which Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has forbidden. Whoever commits it, let him conceal himself with the covering of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. (For whoever exposes his side to us, we will enforce the Book of Allah upon him)."
"1584","[AI-translation] From Sa'id bin Sa'd bin 'Ubadah who said: There was among our dwellings a man who was stunted and weak. He was not noticed until he was upon a slave girl from the slave girls of the house, committing an evil act with her. Sa'd bin 'Ubadah raised his case to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said: Flog him with one hundred lashes. They said: O Prophet of Allah! He is weaker than that; if we strike him one hundred lashes he will die. He said: Take for him a bunch containing one hundred twigs and strike him with it a single strike."
"1585","[AI-translation] Rahman who said: 'Ali delivered a sermon and said: O people! Establish the prescribed punishment upon your slaves, whoever among them is married [and whoever is not married], for a slave girl belonging to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, committed fornication, and he ordered me to flog her. But she had recently given birth, so I feared that if I flogged her I would kill her. I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: You did well. (Leave her until she recovers)."
"1586","[AI-translation] Rahman who said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: O people! Whichever slave or slave-girl commits illicit sexual intercourse, establish the prescribed punishment upon them... Then he said: A servant of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, gave birth from fornication, so he sent me to flog her. I found her to have recently given birth, so I feared (if I were to flog her) that I would kill her. He said: You did well. (Leave her until she recovers)."
"1587","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When you disagree regarding the road, its width should be made seven cubits."
"1588","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: ""When a slave fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he will have two rewards."
"1589","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, raised to the Prophet: ""When the newborn gives a cry, it is inherited from."
"1590","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, raised to the Prophet: ""If one of you insists on an oath regarding his family, he is sinful before Allah regarding the expiation which He has commanded him."
"1591","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, who said: ""When morning comes, Iblis dispatches his troops and says: 'Whoever misleads a Muslim today, I will crown him.'"" He said: ""So this one goes out and says: 'I did not leave him alone until he divorced his wife.' He (Iblis) says: 'He is about to remarry.' And this one comes and says: 'I did not leave him alone until he was undutiful to his parents.' He says: 'He is about to honor them.' And this one comes and says: 'I did not leave him alone until he ascribed partners to Allah.' He says: 'You are you!' And this one comes and says: 'I did not leave him alone until he killed.' He says: 'You are you!' and crowns him."
"1592","[AI-translation] From 'Ali, raised to the Prophet: ""If the two disputants sit before you, do not judge between them until you hear from the other as you heard from the first, for if you do that, the judgment will become clear to you."
"1593","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""When you judge, do so with justice, and when you kill, do so in a good manner, for Allah is Good and loves those who do good."
"1594","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""If the female slave commits illegal sexual intercourse, flog her. If she commits illegal sexual intercourse, flog her. If she commits illegal sexual intercourse, flog her. If she commits illegal sexual intercourse, flog her. Then sell her, even for a hair rope."
"1595","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiya bin Abu Sufyan who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""If they drink wine, flog them. Then if they drink, flog them. Then if they drink, flog them. Then if they drink (a fourth time), kill them."
"1596","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: ""When land is divided and demarcated, there is no right of preemption in it."
"1597","[AI-translation] From Hakim bin Hizam who said: Abu 'Ubaida bin al-Jarrah laid hands on a man from the local people over something, so Khalid bin al-Walid spoke to him. It was said to him: ""You have angered the commander."" Khalid said: ""I did not intend to anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: 'The people who will receive the severest punishment from Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who inflicted the severest punishment on people in this world.'"
"1598","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are: a man killed by a prophet, or a man who killed a prophet, an imam of misguidance, and one who mutilates from among the mutilators."
"1599","Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, said: ""I came with my masters intending to migrate until we drew near to Medina. They entered Medina and left me behind them. Severe hunger afflicted me. Some people leaving Medina passed by me and said to me: 'If you entered the city, you could eat from the fruit of its gardens.' So I entered a garden and cut from two date clusters. The owner of the garden came to me and brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and informed him of my story. I was wearing two garments. He said to me: 'Which of them is better?' I pointed to one of them. He said: 'Take it and give the other to the owner of the garden,' and he let me go free."""
"1600","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Overlook the slips of those of dignified bearing, except the prescribed punishments."
"1601","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the best among you? The best among you are those with the longest lives and the best in deeds."
"1602","[AI-translation] Juhani, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses?! The one who brings his testimony before he is asked for it."
"1603","[AI-translation] From Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from one who heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: Verily, the borrowed property is to be returned, the loaned animal is to be returned, the debt is to be repaid, and the guarantor is liable."
"1604","[AI-translation] Bayhaqi said: thirty) of the sons of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, from their fathers, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, who said: Lo, whoever wrongs a covenanter, or degrades him, or burdens him beyond his capacity, or takes something from him without his willing consent, I will be his adversary on the Day of Resurrection."
"1605","[AI-translation] Ahwas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: Lo, no one commits a crime except against himself. A father does not commit a crime against his son, nor a child against his father."
"1606","[AI-translation] From Abu Rimthah who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, with my father. He said: ""Who is this with you?"" He said: ""My son, I bear witness to him."" He said: ""Indeed, you do not commit a crime against him, nor does he commit a crime against you."
"1607","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: The most grievous usury is a man's transgression against the honor of his brother."
"1608","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah: Khuza'ah killed a man from Banu Layth in the year of the Conquest of Mecca, in retaliation for one of their own whom they had killed. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was informed of this, so he mounted his camel and delivered a sermon. He said: ""Allah withheld the killing (or the Elephant — Abu 'Abdullah doubted) from Mecca, and He gave authority over it to His Messenger and the believers. Behold, it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. Behold, it was made lawful for me only for an hour of a day. Behold, this hour of mine is sacred: its thorns are not to be cut, its trees are not to be felled, its fallen things are not to be picked up except by one who announces it. Whoever is killed has the better of two options: either the blood money is paid, or the family of the victim exacts retaliation."" A man from the people of Yemen said: ""Write this for me, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Write for Abu so-and-so."" A man from Quraysh said: ""Except for idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah! For we use it in our houses and graves."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Except for idhkhir."" Al-Walid added: I said to al-Awza'i: ""What is the meaning of his saying: 'Write for me, O Messenger of Allah!'?"" He said: ""This is the sermon which he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."""
"1609","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Verily, Allah has forbidden my nation khamr, maysir, mizr, kubah, and qinin, and He has added the Witr prayer for me."
"1610","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Verily, Allah is with the debtor (meaning: the one in debt) until he repays his debt, as long as it is not in something Allah dislikes. He said: And 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far used to say to his treasurer: Go and procure a debt for me, for I dislike spending a night except that Allah is with me, after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him."
"1611","[AI-translation] Aslami, raised: If you are able to overpower him, kill him, but do not burn him with fire, for only the Lord of the fire punishes with fire."
"1612","[AI-translation] camel belonging to al-Bara' bin 'Azib entered a man's garden and caused damage in it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, decreed: The owners of gardens are responsible for guarding them during the day, and whatever livestock damages at night, its owners are liable."
"1613","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah: The polytheists captured him and his father, and took a promise from them that they would not fight them on the day of Badr. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Fulfill your promise to them, and we seek Allah's help against them."
"1614","On the authority of Abu Shurayh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on the day following the Day of the Conquest saying a statement which my ears heard, my heart retained, and my eyes saw when he spoke it: He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""Indeed, Allah has sanctified Makkah, and the people did not sanctify it. So it is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood therein, nor to cut down a tree therein. If anyone tries to justify fighting therein for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), say to them: Allah permitted His Messenger, but He did not permit you. And He only permitted me therein for an hour of a day, then its sanctity returned today as it was yesterday. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent."""
"1615","[AI-translation] Siddiq who said: O people! You recite this verse: and I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: When the people see a wrongdoer and do not seize him by his hands, Allah is near to enveloping them with a punishment from Him."
"1616","[AI-translation] Hakam who said: We captured some sheep of the enemy, so we plundered them and set up our pots. The Prophet, peace be upon him, passed by the pots and ordered that they be overturned, then he said: Plunder is not lawful."
"1617","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: I am grasping your waists away from the Fire, saying: Beware of Jahannam! Beware of the boundaries! When I die, I will be your forerunner, and your meeting place is at the Hawd; whoever reaches it will prosper. A people will come and be taken to the Left, and I will say: O Lord, my Ummah! It will be said: You do not know what they introduced after you, turning back on their heels in apostasy."
"1618","On the authority of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from a man of the Anṣār: The Anṣārī informed ʿAṭāʾ that he kissed his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was fasting. So he ordered his wife to ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about that. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The Messenger of Allah does that."" She informed her husband, and he said: ""The Prophet is granted concessions in certain matters. Go back to him and say that to him."" So she returned to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""He said: 'The Prophet is granted concessions in certain matters?!'"" He said: ""I am the most God-fearing of you and the most knowledgeable of you regarding the limits of Allah."""
"1619","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, raised: You bring your disputes to me, and I am only a human. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another, and I judge for you based on what I hear from you. So whoever I judge for something of his brother's right, let him not take it, for I am merely cutting for him a piece of the Fire to bring on the Day of Judgment."
"1620","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, raised: I am only a human, and you bring your disputes to me. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another, so I judge for him based on what I hear from him. Whoever I judge for something from his brother's right, let him not take anything, for I am merely cutting for him a piece of the Fire."
"1621","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to him: What do you think of Ju'ayl? He said: I said: A poor man like him among the people. He said: What do you think of so-and-so? I said: A master of the masters of the people. He said: Ju'ayl is better than an earth full, or thousands, or the like of so-and-so. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is like this, yet you do with him what you do? He said: He is the chief of his people, so I seek to win their hearts through him."
"1622","[AI-translation] Rahman bin 'Abdullah from his father who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, on a journey. He went to attend to a need, and we saw a Humrah bird with two chicks. We took her two chicks, so the Humrah came and began to flutter frantically. The Prophet, peace be upon him, came and said: Who bereaved this of its young? Return its young to her. He also saw an ant colony we had burned, and he said: Who burned this? We said: We did. He said: It is not fitting that anyone punish with fire except the Lord of the fire."
"1623","Al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami said: We camped with the Prophet ﷺ at Khaybar, and with him were those of his companions who were with him. The chief of Khaybar was a recalcitrant, defiant man. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Muhammad! Is it lawful for you to slaughter our donkeys, eat our fruits, and strike our women?!"" The Prophet ﷺ became angry and said: ""O Ibn 'Awf! Mount your horse, then announce: 'Verily, Paradise is not lawful except for a believer, and gather for the prayer.'"" So they gathered, then the Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer. Then he stood up and said: ""Does any one of you think, reclining on his couch, that Allah has not forbidden anything except what is in this Qur'an?! No, by Allah, I have indeed commanded, admonished, and forbidden things, and they are like the Qur'an or even more. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not made it lawful for you to enter the houses of the People of the Book except with permission, nor to strike their women, nor to eat their fruits when they have given you what is due upon them."""
"1624","[AI-translation] From Ya'la bin Murra who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: Any man who unjustly takes a handspan of land, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will burden him to dig it until he reaches the end of the seven earths, then it will be draped around his neck until the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed among the people."
"1625","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: Any guest who descends upon a people and the guest is left deprived, it is permissible for him to take according to the measure of his hospitality, and there is no sin upon him."
"1626","[AI-translation] From Khuzayma bin Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Any servant who commits anything that Allah has forbidden, and then his prescribed punishment is carried out upon him, it expiates that sin for him."
"1627","[AI-translation] From Jarir bin Bajila, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, he said: The covenant is absolved from whoever resides among the polytheists in their lands."
"1628","[AI-translation] From Ya'la bin Umayya, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: When my messengers come to you, give them thirty coats of armor and thirty camels. I said: O Messenger of Allah! As a guaranteed loan or a returned loan? He said: ""Rather, as a returned loan."
"1629","[AI-translation] From Asma' bint Umays, that she said: When Ja'far bin Abi Talib was afflicted, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, commanded me, saying: Observe mourning for three days, then do whatever you wish."
"1630","[AI-translation] From Umm Hani: That she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: Will we visit each other when we die, and will some of us see each other? The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The souls will be birds clinging to the trees until the Day of Resurrection, when every soul will enter its body."
"1631","[AI-translation] From Ubayy bin Ka'b, raised to the Prophet: ""The two previously-married persons are flogged and stoned, and the two virgins are flogged and banished."
"1632","[AI-translation] Bajali, raised to the Prophet: A man among those before you suffered a wound. He grew distressed by it, took a knife, and slit his hand with it. The blood did not cease from him until he died. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: My servant preempted Me with his soul; I have forbidden Paradise to him."
"1633","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: A prescribed punishment carried out on earth is better for the people of the earth than that they be rained upon for forty mornings."
"1634","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The protective boundary of a well is forty cubits around it, all of it for the resting places of camels and sheep."
"1635","[AI-translation] Sha'bi, raised [to the Prophet]: He passed by the companions of the dirdakah and said: Carry on, O Banu Arfidah! So that the Jews and Christians may know that there is spaciousness in our religion. He said: While they were thus, 'Umar came, and when they saw him they scattered."
"1636","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, raised to the Prophet: Khamr is the mother of all evils, and whoever drinks it, Allah will not accept his prayer for forty days. If he dies while it is in his stomach, he dies a death of Jahiliyyah."
"1637","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, raised [to the Prophet]: Khamr is the mother of abominations and the greatest of major sins; whoever drinks it will commit incest with his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt."
"1638","[AI-translation] Ghifari who said: A questioner asked the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saying: O Messenger of Allah! What if someone attacks me? The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to him: Remind him of Allah three times. If he refuses, then fight him. If he kills you, you are in Paradise, and if you kill him, he is in the Fire."
"1639","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The covenant of the Muslims is one; if a transgressor transgresses against them, do not betray it. For every traitor will have a banner by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection."
"1640","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir from the Prophet, peace be upon him: Raisins and dates are khamr (meaning when they are both infused together)."
"1641","[AI-translation] 'Ajma', the maternal aunt of Abu Umamah bin Sahl. The hadith of 'Umar from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: 'Umar said: I fear that a time will grow long for the people until a speaker says: We do not find stoning in the Book of Allah, and they will go astray by abandoning an obligation Allah revealed. Verily, stoning is true if one is married, or the evidence is established, or there is pregnancy, or confession. And I recited it: ""The old man and the old woman..."" [to the end of] the hadith. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, stoned, and we stoned after him."
"1642","[AI-translation] Jarud, raised [to the Prophet]: The stray animal of a Muslim is the fuel of the Fire."
"1643","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The loaned animal is to be compensated, the gifted animal is to be returned, and whoever finds a tied lost item, it is not lawful for him to untie it until he shows it."
"1644","[AI-translation] From Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, marfu': Fighting a believer is disbelief and reviling him is immorality, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to shun his brother for more than three days."
"1645","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, whenever he swore an oath, would not break it until Allah, Exalted be He, revealed the expiation for an oath. He then said: I shall not swear an oath and see something better than it, except that I expiate my oath and then come to that which is better."
"1646","[AI-translation] From Shahr bin Hawshab, he said: I said to Umm Salama: O Mother of the Believers! What was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, when he was with you? She said: His most frequent supplication was: O Turner of the hearts! Keep my heart firm upon Your religion. He was asked about that, so he said: There is no child of Adam except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; if He wills He keeps it upright, and if He wills He causes it to deviate."
"1647","[AI-translation] Juhani, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, whenever he swore an oath, would say: By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad."
"1648","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Umar: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, divorced Hafsa, then took her back."
"1649","On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take a hair from the side of a camel from the spoils of war and say: ""I have no more right to it than any one of you. Beware of misappropriating spoils (ghulul), for misappropriation is a disgrace for its perpetrator on the Day of Resurrection. Render the thread and the needle and whatever is above that. Strive in the cause of Allah, the Exalted, near and far, in residence and in travel, for jihad is a gate from the gates of Paradise. Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saves through it from worry and grief. Establish the limits of Allah near and far, and let not the blame of a blamer deter you in Allah's cause."""
"1650","[AI-translation] 'Irbad: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, would take a tuft of wool from the spoils of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and say: I have of this nothing but the like of what any of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return the thread and the needle and whatever is above them, and beware of plundering! For it is disgrace and ignominy upon its possessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"1651","[AI-translation] From 'Ubayd Allah bin 'Abdullah (bin 'Utbah) from his father: That Subay'ah bint al-Harith became pure from her postpartum bleeding days after the death of her husband. Abu al-Sanabil passed by her and said: You are not lawful until you wait four months and ten. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: Abu al-Sanabil has lied; it is not as he said. You have become lawful, so marry (when someone you are pleased with comes to you, then come to me or inform me)."
"1652","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: A strike with a whip is sufficient for you against a snake, whether you hit it or miss it."
"1653","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden. Whoever drinks an intoxicant, his prayer is rejected for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he repeats it a fourth time, it is a right upon Allah to make him drink from the mud of Khabal. It was said: What is the mud of Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire. And whoever gives it to a child who does not know its lawful from its unlawful, it is a right upon Allah to make him drink from the mud of Khabal."
"1654","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, he says: 'Umar bin al-Khattab informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: I will surely expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until I leave none but Muslims."
"1655","[AI-translation] Khattab, ascribed to the Prophet: ""If I live, God willing, I will indeed forbid that one be named Rabah, Najih, Aflah, Nafi`, and Yasar."
"1656","[AI-translation] Miqdad bin Al-Aswad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said to his companions: ""What do you say about adultery?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) then said: ""For a man to commit adultery with ten women is lighter upon him than committing adultery with his neighbor's wife."" Then he asked them about theft, and they answered similarly to what they answered about adultery. Then he said: ""And for a man to steal from ten houses is lighter upon him than stealing from his neighbor."
"1657","[AI-translation] From Ma`qil bin Yasar, ascribed to the Prophet: ""For an iron needle to be driven into the head of a man is better for him than touching a woman who is not lawful for him."
"1658","[AI-translation] From Ibn `Abbas, ascribed to the Prophet: ""He repented with such a repentance that had the collector of tolls repented with it, it would have been accepted from him."
"1659","[AI-translation] From Zaid bin Thabit who said: When this verse which is in Al-Furqan was revealed: ""And those who invoke not any other god along with Allah, nor kill such life as Allah has forbidden, except for just cause..."", we were amazed by its explanation, so we remained for six months. Then the verse in An-Nisa was revealed: ""And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein, and the wrath of Allah is on him, and He has cursed him and prepared for him a grievous torment"" (93), until it ended."
"1660","[AI-translation] From Nu`aym bin Hazzal from his father that Ma`iz came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and confessed before him four times, so he ordered that he be stoned, and said to Hazzal: ""Had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you."
"1661","[AI-translation] From Talhah, ascribed to the Prophet: ""There is no retaliation for the head wound exposing the membrane."
"1662","[AI-translation] From `Abdullah bin `Amr, ascribed to the Prophet: ""He is not of us who imitates others. Do not imitate the Jews or the Christians, for the greeting of the Jews is gesturing with the fingers, and the greeting of the Christians is gesturing with the palms."
"1663","[AI-translation] Darda' (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: He said: ""What Allah has made lawful in His Book is lawful, and what He has forbidden is forbidden, and what He was silent about is forgiven, so accept Allah's pardon."
"1664","[AI-translation] From `Abdullah bin Mu`awiyah bin Hudayj who informed him that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is lawful for me of what is forbidden upon me?"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) remained silent. He repeated it three times, each time the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) remaining silent. He then said: ""Who is the questioner?"" The man said: ""It is me, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said, pointing with his two fingers: ""What your heart denies, leave it."
"1665","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no ruler except that he has two close circles: one commanding him to good and forbidding him from evil, and one that spares no effort in corrupting him. Whoever is protected from its evil has indeed been protected, and he is from whichever of the two overcomes him."
"1666","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no ruler except that he has two close circles: one commanding him to good and forbidding him from evil, and one that spares no effort in corrupting him. Whoever is protected from its evil has indeed been protected, and he is from whichever of the two overcomes him."
"1667","On the authority of An-Nu'man bin Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: ""The parable of the one who upholds the limits of Allah and the one who violates them (and in a narration: and the one who grazes near them) (and the one who is complacent regarding them) is like the parable of a people who drew lots for a ship (in the sea). So some of them got its upper deck, and some of them got its lower deck (and its most rugged part). So those who were in the lower deck, when they drew water, they passed by those above them (causing them harm) (and in a narration: so those in the lower deck would ascend to draw water and pour it on those in the upper deck, so those in the upper deck said: 'We will not let you ascend and harm us'). So they said: 'If we were to bore a hole in our section (and draw water from it) and not harm those above us' (and in a narration: 'and not pass by our companions and harm them'). So he took an axe and began to chip away at the bottom of the ship. They came to him and said: 'What is the matter with you?' He said: 'You were harmed by me, and I have no alternative but to get water.' So if they left them to do what they intended, they would all perish, and if they restrained them, they would all be saved and save others."""
"1668","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Bakrah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever honors the authority of Allah, Allah will honor him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1669","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever revives dead land has a reward for it, and whatever the animals eat from it is a reward for him."
"1670","[AI-translation] Thaqafi: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Whoever takes land unjustly will be burdened to carry its soil to the gathering place."
"1671","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Whoever claims lineage to other than his father will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance can be detected from a distance of seventy years."
"1672","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Amr, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever is entrusted with a trust, there is no liability upon him."
"1673","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him and his family: If a man embraces Islam at his hands, then he is his Mawla."
"1674","[AI-translation] Narrated Khuzaymah ibn Thabit from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Whoever commits a sin and the prescribed punishment for that sin is enforced upon him, it is his expiation."
"1675","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: Whoever aids a wrongdoer with falsehood to invalidate truth with his falsehood has absolved himself from the covenant of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the covenant of His Messenger."
"1676","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Umar (marfu'an): Whoever aids a disputant with injustice, or aids in injustice, remains in the wrath of Allah until he ceases."
"1677","[AI-translation] Narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever grants life tenure of something, it belongs to the one granted it for his life and his death. And do not expect its return; whoever expects the return of something, it is his path."" And in a narration: ""The path of inheritance."
"1678","On the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched ʿAlqamah ibn Mujazzir on a military expedition, and I was among them. When he reached the farthest point of his campaign—or at some point along the way—a group from the army sought his permission [to separate], so he granted them permission and appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥudhāfah ibn Qays al-Sahmī as their commander. I was among those who went on the expedition with him. At some point along the way, the people kindled a fire to warm themselves or to cook something on it. ʿAbdullāh said—and he was given to jesting—""Do I not have the right to your hearing and obedience?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then am I not such that whatever I command you, you do it?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then I strictly enjoin upon you that you throw yourselves into this fire."" Some men stood up, restraining themselves [from jumping]. When he thought they were about to jump, he said: ""Hold back! I was only joking with you."" When we returned, they mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever among your rulers commands you to disobey [Allah], do not obey him."""
"1679","[AI-translation] Qitbani who said: Were it not for a word I heard from 'Amr ibn al-Hamiq al-Khuza'i, I would have walked between the head of al-Mukhtar and his body. I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever gives a man safety for his life and then kills him, he will carry the banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."
"1680","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever disowns his child to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of witnesses, recompense for recompense."
"1681","[AI-translation] Narrated from some of the Companions of Muhammad who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever spends the night on top of a roof that has no parapet and falls and dies, the responsibility is absolved from him; and whoever rides the sea when it is turbulent and dies, the responsibility is absolved from him."
"1682","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir (marfu'an): Whoever takes as guardians other than his guardians has stripped the ring of faith from his neck."
"1683","[AI-translation] Narrated from Samurah ibn Jundub (marfu'an): ""Whoever associates with a polytheist and dwells with him, he is like him."
"1684","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Abbas (marfu'an): Whoever incites against horses on the day of racing is not from us."
"1685","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar (marfu'an): ""Whoever's intercession prevents a prescribed punishment from the punishments of Allah has opposed Allah in His command. And whoever dies while indebted, there are no dinars nor dirhams there, but rather it is good deeds and bad deeds. And whoever disputes in falsehood while knowing, he remains in the wrath of Allah until he ceases. And whoever says about a believer what is not in him, he will be detained in the mire of destruction until he brings an exit from what he said."
"1686","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Imran ibn Husayn (marfu'an): Whoever swears a deceptive oath falsely (deliberately), let him take his seat in the Fire with his face."
"1687","[AI-translation] From Aishah, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever swears an oath to sever ties of kinship or regarding something improper, his righteousness is not to fulfill it."
"1688","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever of my Ummah incurs a debt, then struggles to repay it but dies without repaying it, I am his guarantor."
"1689","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever drinks wine in this world and does not repent will not drink it in the Hereafter, even if he enters Paradise."
"1690","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Whoever intercedes for his brother with an intercession, and is given a gift for it which he accepts, has come to a great door among the doors of Riba."
"1691","[AI-translation] Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever draws his sword and then puts it down, his blood is spilled without retribution."
"1692","[AI-translation] From Ammar bin Yasir, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever unjustly beats his slave, retaliation will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1693","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever kills a covenanted person without right, he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and indeed the fragrance of Paradise is detected from a distance of a hundred years' journey."
"1694","[AI-translation] From Sulaym bin Amir, he says: There was a treaty between Muawiyah and the Romans, and he was marching through their land until, when the treaty expired, he raided them. And there was a man on a mount or on a horse saying: ""Allah is the Greatest, fulfilling the treaty, not betrayal!"" (twice). And it was Amr bin Abasah al-Sulami. Muawiyah said to him: ""What are you saying?"" Amr said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: 'Whoever has a treaty between himself and a people must neither untie its knot nor fasten it until its term expires or he renounces it to them on equal terms.'"
"1695","[AI-translation] From Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: ""Whoever is in debt intending to repay it, there will be with him help from Allah, and Allah will facilitate provision for him."
"1696","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Whoever passes by a garden, let him eat and not carry away."
"1697","On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: When the Day of Uhud came, sixty-four men from the Ansar were killed, and six from the Muhajirun. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""If we have a day like this against the polytheists, we will surely exact a greater retribution from them."" Then when the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah) came, a man who was not recognized said: ""No Quraysh after today."" So the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) proclaimed: ""Is there safety for the black and the white except so-and-so and so-and-so?"" naming certain people. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ""And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you endure patiently, verily it is better for the patient."" (An-Nahl: 126). So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""We endure patiently and we do not punish."""
"1698","[AI-translation] From Zayd ibn Thabit, marfu': He forbade mukhabarah. I said: And what is mukhabarah? He said: That you take the land for half, a third, or a quarter."
"1699","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""Fire is absolved of liability."
"1700","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""I gave my mother a garden of mine, and she died and left no heir other than me."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Your charity is accepted, and your garden has returned to you."
"1701","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The child of zina is the worst of the three."
"1702","Abū Mājida reported: I was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) when he said: ""I remember the first man whose hand was cut off by the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). A thief was brought to him and he ordered his hand to be cut off. It was as if the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) changed. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! It seems you disliked cutting it off?' He said: 'And what prevents me? Do not be helpers to Satan against your brother. Indeed, it is not appropriate for the Imam when a ḥadd punishment reaches him except to establish it. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and loves forgiveness.' And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful (22) (An-Nūr)."""
"1703","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, marfu': ""The weight is the weight of the people of Makkah, and the measure is the measure of the people of Madinah."
"1704","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, marfu': The child is from the earnings of the parent."
"1705","[AI-translation] From Umayyah ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) borrowed armor from him on the day of Hunayn. He said: ""Is it by force, O Muhammad?"" He replied: ""No, rather it is a guaranteed loan."
"1706","[AI-translation] Muharibi, marfu': A mother does not commit an offense against a child, a mother does not commit an offense against a child."
"1707","[AI-translation] Khashkhash al-Anbari, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) with a son of mine. He said: He asked: ""Is this your son?"" He said: I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Do not commit an offense against him, and he should not commit an offense against you."
"1708","[AI-translation] From Usamah ibn Sharik, marfu': No soul commits an offense against another."
"1709","[AI-translation] Fadl, she said: A Bedouin entered upon the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, while he was in my house, and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! I had a wife, and I married another in addition to her. My first wife claimed that she had suckled my new wife a suckle or two."" The Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""One suckling and two sucklings do not prohibit."
"1710","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, came with two young boys, and he gifted one of them to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: ""Do not beat him, for I have been forbidden from beating those who pray, and I saw him praying since we approached."" And he gave a young boy to Abu Dharr and said: ""Treat him well."" So he freed him. He said: ""What did you do?"" He said: ""You commanded me to treat him well, so I freed him."
"1711","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Jafar, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, passed by some people who were shooting arrows at a ram, and he disliked that and said: ""Do not mutilate animals."
"1712","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""There is no harm and no reciprocating of harm."
"1713","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, took the hand of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and went with him to his son Ibrahim. He found him breathing his last. So the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, took him and placed him in his lap, and wept. Abd al-Rahman said to him: ""Are you weeping? Did you not forbid weeping?"" He said: ""No, but I forbade two foolish, wicked sounds: a sound at a calamity of scratching faces and tearing garments, and the howling of the devil."
"1714","[AI-translation] Miswar ibn Makhramah, raised to the Prophet: A child does not inherit until he cries out at birth, and his crying out is that he screams, or sneezes, or weeps."
"1715","[AI-translation] Ahwas, from his mother (Umm Jundub), she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, throwing the Jamrah from the bottom of the valley while he was riding, pronouncing takbir with every pebble. And a man was behind him shielding him. I asked about the man, and they said: ""al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas."" The people crowded around, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Let none of you kill one another, and let none of you strike one another. And when you throw the Jamrah, throw with pebbles like those of khadhf."
"1716","[AI-translation] Khudri, raised to the Prophet: Let not the awe of people prevent a man from speaking the truth if he knows it (or witnesses it, or hears it)."
"1717","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: The flogged fornicator does not marry except his like."
"1718","[AI-translation] Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, delivering a sermon in Medina, saying: ""O people, Allah the Exalted is making an allusion regarding wine, and perhaps Allah will soon reveal a command concerning it. So whoever has any of it with him, let him sell it and benefit from it."" We did not wait long before the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Allah the Exalted has forbidden wine. So whoever this verse reaches and he has any of it with him, let him neither drink it nor sell it."
"1719","[AI-translation] Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) led us in prayer on the day of Hunayn beside a camel from the divided spoils, then he reached for something from the camel and took from it a piece of fur—he meant: a tuft of hair—and placed it between his fingers, then he said: ""O people! This is from your spoils. Deliver the thread and the needle, and whatever is above that and whatever is below that. For indeed, the act of stealing from the spoils is a disgrace upon its possessor on the Day of Resurrection, and a shame, and a fire."
"1720","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, elevated to the Prophet: A man will come holding another man by the hand and say: ""O Lord! This one killed me."" Allah will say to him: ""Why did you kill him?"" He will say: ""I killed him so that honor might be Yours."" He will say: ""Indeed it is Mine."" And a man will come holding another man by the hand and say: ""Indeed, this one killed me."" Allah will say to him: ""Why did you kill him?"" He will say: ""So that honor might be for so-and-so!"" He will say: ""Indeed, it is not for so-and-so."" And he will bear his sin."
